# Git for Windows checks out text files as CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true).
# Common Lisp's FORMAT line-continuation directive is a tilde immediately
# followed by a newline; under CRLF the next character is a carriage return
# instead, so FORMAT rejects it as an unknown directive and the file fails to
# compile. Pinning LF keeps every tracked text file byte-identical on all
# platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf
